----+Here is compact Cursor-oriented review feedback.
----+
----+High-value fixes first
----+	1.	CacheExplicit semantics are wrong
----+	•	Current behavior of CacheExplicit == CacheLazy in practice.
----+	•	Both auto-populate cache on first read via cachedLDs / cachedItems.
----+	•	If the intended contract is:
----+	•	CacheNone: always hit server
----+	•	CacheLazy: auto-fill transparently
----+	•	CacheExplicit: use cache only after explicit refresh/fill/invalidate cycle
----+	•	then CacheExplicit is not implemented yet.
----+	•	Fix: gate implicit setLDs / setItems / setDS behind strategy check, or define explicit prefill methods and only consult cache in explicit mode when already populated.
----+	2.	Dataset cache returns mutable shared pointers
----+	•	modelCache.getDS() returns the cached *DataSet directly.
----+	•	Caller can mutate Members, Reference, etc. and corrupt cache globally.
----+	•	Fix: deep-copy DataSet on getDS and setDS like you already do for LDs/items.
----+	3.	Report subscription dispatch only supports one subscriber per report
----+	•	reportSubs map[string]*ReportSubscription
----+	•	findSubscription() returns only one match.
----+	•	Problems:
----+	•	second subscribe with same RptID/pattern overwrites first
----+	•	multiple glob subscriptions do not all receive matching reports
----+	•	exact + glob subscriber cannot both receive same report
----+	•	Requirement-wise, this is too restrictive.
----+	•	Fix: store map[string][]*ReportSubscription or flat set/list, dispatch to all matching subscribers.
----+	4.	Timestamp encode path is stale after go-mms quality-byte support
----+	•	DecodeTimestamp() now reads UTCTimeQuality(), good.
----+	•	EncodeTimestamp() still uses mms.NewUTCTime(ts.Time) and drops quality.
----+	•	Comment is also outdated and now false.
----+	•	Fix: use go-mms constructor with quality byte if available, and update docs/tests.
----+	•	Add roundtrip test for non-zero TimeQuality.
----+	5.	SCL generation drops Services
----+	•	parse.go fully parses Services.
----+	•	generate.go / iedToXML() never writes Services back.
----+	•	So SCL roundtrip is incomplete and silently lossy.
----+	•	Fix: add servicesToXML() and populate xmlIED.Services.
----+	•	Add roundtrip test asserting Services survives.
----+
----+⸻
----+
----+Medium-priority correctness gaps
----+	6.	Report dispatch + glob matching should probably fan out, not first-match
----+	•	Even if you keep exact-match fast path, matching logic should deliver to every exact/glob subscriber, not first hit.
----+	7.	OverflowBlock can stall shutdown/dispatch
----+	•	deliver() blocks while holding sub.mu.
----+	•	If channel is full and consumer is stalled, close/unsubscribe can also stall behind the same lock.
----+	•	Not necessarily wrong, but risky.
----+	•	Safer: do not hold sub.mu across blocking send, or document that OverflowBlock may block shutdown.
----+	8.	Segmented report reassembly is minimal
----+	•	No validation of contiguous SubSeqNum.
----+	•	Mismatched/interleaved segment streams reset buffer silently.
----+	•	Good first pass, but not robust enough for noisy real devices.
----+	•	At least log resets / sequence mismatch.
----+	9.	GetDataSet() cache is used, but ReadDataSet() still re-fetches attrs every time
----+	•	Not a correctness bug, but it leaves some caching value on the table.
----+	•	If dataset-definition caching is part of the pre-server contract, ReadDataSet() should reuse cached definition when available.
----+	10.	CreateDataSet() input validation is weaker than its docs
----+
----+	•	Docs say member Ref should include LD/LN/FC.
----+	•	Implementation only relies on Validate() + ToMMS(), so LN-level refs could sneak in.
----+	•	Fix: require m.Ref.LN != "" && m.Ref.FC != "" and likely m.Ref.IsObject() when deriving from Ref.
----+
----+⸻
----+
----+Smaller notes
----+	11.	checkOpen() should use RLock
----+
----+	•	Minor perf/style only.
----+
----+	12.	RefreshCache() leaves partial cache on mid-refresh failure
----+
----+	•	If one LD fetch fails after LD list was stored, cache can be partially rebuilt.
----+	•	Better: build fresh temp snapshot, then swap in atomically.
----+
----+	13.	SCL validation is still relatively shallow
----+
----+	•	Good baseline, but network-aware validation still looks partial:
----+	•	no GSE/SMV LDInst / CBName cross-checks
----+	•	no dataset member target validation
----+	•	no report-to-dataset/member consistency beyond local dataset name warning
----+	•	Not a bug, but still not “serious tooling complete”.
----+
----+	14.	ReadComponent() is path-append based, not true component read
----+
----+	•	API is fine and go-mms agnostic.
----+	•	Just be aware this is semantic sugar over full-path read, not MMS component-optimized read.
